num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-06T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"veAVEqfHk","title":"Improving PHP Performance for Web Applications","url":"https://www.keycdn.com/blog/php-performance","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/improving-php-performance-for-web-applications-veaveqfhk","summary":"The best tool for improving PHP performance isn't any individual program; it's knowing which problems to look for and how to address them. Achieving optimal performance is often a balancing act that requires trade-offs between speed, accuracy, and scalability. Writing good code is the essential step to creating PHP applications that are fast and stable.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1c75c91288dcd4e8bcc9b41ff0dd0184?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":26,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-05-18T06:28:45.000Z"},{"id":"BsMwQM8qr","title":"Microservices vs APIs: What's the Difference","url":"https://www.keycdn.com/blog/microservices-vs-apis","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/microservices-vs-apis-what-s-the-difference-bsmwqm8qr","summary":"The only two solutions that strike first in every individual's mind are Microservices and APIs. These solutions are gaining popularity in the world of software development because of the constantly growing requirement to produce scalable, flexible, and secure applications at quicker turnaround times. But there is great confusion between these two, and they can never be sure which solution would be best.","image":"https://www.keycdn.com/img/blog/microservices-vs-apis.png","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-27T06:30:00.000Z"},{"id":"jSxouDI0f","title":"Website Security Check: How to Secure Your Website","url":"https://www.keycdn.com/blog/website-security-check","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/website-security-check-how-to-secure-your-website-jsxoudi0f","summary":"The tide of web attacks, and thus compromised data, continues to rise. Up to 120 million cyber attacks are currently recorded every day. In 2019, over 60% of websites were vulnerable at the time of infection. Hacking is vast, but which are the most common vulnerabilities hackers take advantage of.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/50e8b9e8a86c086d8453fc6d5e0b5ba5","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-24T08:23:03.661Z"},{"id":"IlbmiksDU","title":"Web Development Trends","url":"https://www.keycdn.com/blog/web-development-trends","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/web-development-trends-ilbmiksdu","summary":"Smart developers are always looking ahead for ways to adapt to the ever-changing world of web development. Progressive web apps (PWA) are web applications that look and feel like native mobile apps but can be accessed through a web browser. Chatbots and virtual assistants are becoming more common on websites and web applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/111b4b5f2c47e0695bd26a14838b3aad","num_upvotes":38,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2023-03-01T11:17:53.896Z"},{"id":"jsIlHIse-","title":"KeyCDN Launches New POPs in 2023","url":"https://www.keycdn.com/blog/pops-in-2023","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/keycdn-launches-new-pops-in-2023-jsilhise","summary":"KeyCDN launches 4 new points of presence (POPs) in 2023. Namely, Copenhagen, Dublin, Lisbon, and Lima have been added. The new POPs are in production and have been automatically added to all existing Zones. With a dedicated POP, latency for visitors is reduced even further.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/be022e9f69741ca02ba4c13b3c815ec0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-26T11:00:42.423Z"},{"id":"Ym7MjOATB","title":"Why is Wordpress Slow?","url":"https://www.keycdn.com/blog/wordpress-slow","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-is-wordpress-slow--ym7mjoatb","summary":"A WordPress website c